WEBVTT

00:00:09,490 --> 00:00:10,770
Hello, thank you for your help.

00:00:10,770 --> 00:00:14,010
I would like to help a friend with our rife machine.

00:00:14,010 --> 00:00:17,130
Are there any specific programs that you'd suggest

00:00:17,130 --> 00:00:21,530
for neuropathy in their legs and feet?

00:00:23,490 --> 00:00:25,410
Yeah, the neuropathy program.

00:00:25,410 --> 00:00:29,690
So there's neuropathy programs in the true rife folder.

00:00:29,690 --> 00:00:33,250
There's neuropathy programs in the atelier robin folder.

00:00:33,250 --> 00:00:36,210
So either one of those could be helpful,

00:00:36,210 --> 00:00:39,050
but always with any disease,

00:00:39,050 --> 00:00:42,970
you always want to ask that one question, why?

00:00:42,970 --> 00:00:45,290
So why do they have neuropathy?

00:00:45,290 --> 00:00:47,330
Do they have diabetic neuropathy?

00:00:47,330 --> 00:00:49,490
Do they have keyboard booster apathy?

00:00:50,650 --> 00:00:52,250
Those are the things that you want to,

00:00:52,250 --> 00:00:54,610
because you really want to deal with the cause, right?

00:00:54,610 --> 00:00:58,530
So if the person has diabetic neuropathy,

00:00:58,530 --> 00:01:01,490
well, you certainly can use the rife neuropathy programs,

00:01:01,490 --> 00:01:05,690
but if you don't deal with the diabetes,

00:01:05,690 --> 00:01:08,690
you're not going to really be ultimately helping that person.

00:01:08,690 --> 00:01:12,250
If the person has neuropathy because they did chemo a year ago,

00:01:12,250 --> 00:01:13,450
and they're done with that,

00:01:13,450 --> 00:01:17,050
but now they have this neuropathy within my all means,

00:01:17,050 --> 00:01:18,210
just jump into this,

00:01:18,210 --> 00:01:22,890
then the causative factor is done.

00:01:22,890 --> 00:01:25,250
You don't have to make changes there.

00:01:25,250 --> 00:01:29,130
Also, detoxine as much as possible can be helpful

00:01:29,130 --> 00:01:31,610
if it's something like that.

00:01:31,610 --> 00:01:33,210
Not diabetes, but chemo therapy,

00:01:33,210 --> 00:01:36,890
because chemo therapy induced neuropathy is from basically

00:01:36,890 --> 00:01:39,090
the toxicity of the chemo therapy,

00:01:39,090 --> 00:01:41,450
actually killing the nerves.

00:01:42,650 --> 00:01:45,810
So helping detox would be helpful, too.

00:01:47,010 --> 00:01:48,770
Sorry, I shouldn't have read the rest of the questions.

00:01:48,770 --> 00:01:50,170
She said she's not diabetic,

00:01:50,170 --> 00:01:51,970
and it's not from heavy metals.

00:01:51,970 --> 00:01:55,250
It was diagnosed as unspecified neuropathy.

00:01:55,250 --> 00:01:59,410
She also has two bad knees that the doctors say need replacing.

00:02:01,810 --> 00:02:04,450
So still, I mean, she's got to get diagnosed.

00:02:04,890 --> 00:02:07,010
There's some causes of neuropathy.

00:02:08,170 --> 00:02:11,650
If it's in the hands and the feet,

00:02:11,650 --> 00:02:13,530
or it's in her legs and her feet,

00:02:14,410 --> 00:02:17,250
then it certainly could be just neurological

00:02:17,250 --> 00:02:22,250
because of blood flow.

00:02:22,850 --> 00:02:27,450
You do a full differential diagnosis

00:02:27,450 --> 00:02:32,210
as the person have heart issues if they have weakness

00:02:32,210 --> 00:02:33,050
in their heart.

00:02:33,050 --> 00:02:36,490
It might not be getting good blood flow to their legs,

00:02:36,490 --> 00:02:38,450
especially if she's got two bad knees

00:02:38,450 --> 00:02:40,650
that could be blocking blood flow.

00:02:40,650 --> 00:02:42,290
There could be stasis.

00:02:42,290 --> 00:02:43,810
Even if the person has diabetes,

00:02:43,810 --> 00:02:45,490
you could still have sugar stasis

00:02:45,490 --> 00:02:46,970
in the lower extremities.

00:02:48,210 --> 00:02:51,730
So that could be the cause of it.

00:02:51,730 --> 00:02:56,010
Certainly looking at the rebuilder would be helpful, too,

00:02:56,010 --> 00:02:57,810
but if you don't deal with the cause,

00:02:57,810 --> 00:02:59,730
then that's not going to really be the answer.

00:02:59,730 --> 00:03:01,930
But definitely, I would definitely use the right.

00:03:01,930 --> 00:03:02,930
That's for sure.

